id: real-estate
name: Real estate and property management
industry: Real estate & construction
domain: Property sales, leasing and management
scope: Properties, buildings and units, owners, listings, enquiries and viewings, sale transactions, leases and tenants, rent and service charges, maintenance requests, valuations.
summary: Describes property and what happens to it commercially: what exists and who owns it, how it is listed, shown and sold or let, what rent is due and paid, and how it is maintained. A starter model following the RESO Data Dictionary for listings and the Building Topology Ontology for structure.
purpose: Shared vocabulary across listing, leasing and facilities systems; basis for occupancy, yield and arrears analytics.
read: A Property contains Buildings and Units and is owned by an Owner. A Listing offers a unit for sale or rent through an Agent; Enquiries and Viewings follow. A Sale transaction transfers it to a buyer; a Lease lets a unit to a Tenant, generating Rent charges settled by Rent payments. Maintenance requests are raised on units; Valuations record worth.
in: Property structure and ownership; Listings, enquiries, viewings; Sales; Leases and rent; Maintenance; Valuation
out: Construction project management; Mortgage lending; Land registry procedures; Facility energy management
std: realestate | high | Listing, property, member and office concepts follow the RESO Data Dictionary; lease concepts follow OSCRE. | Property, Listing, Member, Office, Lease
std: ifc | medium | Site, building, storey and space structure follows the Building Topology Ontology (BOT) / IFC. | bot:Building, bot:Storey, bot:Space
std: schema | medium | Places, offers and agents are aligned to schema.org. | schema:Residence, schema:RealEstateAgent, schema:Offer
std: geosparql | low | Locations follow GeoSPARQL. | geo:Feature
== Property | Property | What exists.
Property | A parcel of land with whatever is built on it.
  - property code : string !
  - name : string
  - address : string !
  - city : string
  - land area sqm : decimal
  - latitude : decimal
  - longitude : decimal
  > owned by > Owner +
  > of type > PropertyType 1
PropertyType | The use of a property.
  * Residential, Office, Retail, Industrial, Land, Mixed use
Building | A structure on a property.
  - name : string !
  - floors : integer
  - built year : gYear
  > on property > Property 1
Unit | A separately sellable or lettable space, such as a flat, shop or office suite.
  - unit number : string !
  - floor : integer
  - area sqm : decimal !
  - bedrooms : integer
  - furnished : boolean
  > in building > Building 1 | | has unit
  > has status > UnitStatus 1
UnitStatus | Whether a unit is occupied or available.
  * Vacant, Listed, Let, Sold, Under maintenance
Owner | A person or company holding title to a property.
  - name : string !
  - contact number : string
== Market | Listings and viewings | Finding buyers and tenants.
Agent | A person who markets property for owners. | ~schema:RealEstateAgent
  - name : string !
  - licence number : string
  - agency : string
Listing | An offer of a unit for sale or rent.
  - listing number : string !
  - listed on : date !
  - asking price : decimal !
  - closed on : date
  > of unit > Unit 1
  > by agent > Agent 1
  > for purpose > ListingPurpose 1
  > has status > ListingStatus 1
ListingPurpose | Whether the unit is offered for sale or to let.
  * Sale, Rent
ListingStatus | The state of a listing.
  * Active, Under offer, Closed, Withdrawn, Expired
Enquiry | An expression of interest in a listing.
  - received on : date !
  - name : string
  - source : string
  > about > Listing 1 | | receives enquiry
Viewing | A visit by a prospect to a listed unit.
  - held at : dateTime !
  - feedback : string
  > of listing > Listing 1
  > from enquiry > Enquiry ?
  > hosted by > Agent ?
== Deal | Sales and leases | Transfer and letting.
SaleTransaction | The sale of a unit to a buyer.
  - agreed on : date !
  - completed on : date
  - sale price : decimal !
  - buyer name : string !
  > of unit > Unit 1
  > from listing > Listing ?
Tenant | A person or company that rents a unit.
  - name : string !
  - contact number : string
  - email : string
Lease | An agreement letting a unit to a tenant for a period at a rent.
  - lease number : string !
  - start date : date !
  - end date : date !
  - monthly rent : decimal !
  - deposit : decimal
  - escalation percent : decimal
  > of unit > Unit 1 | | let under
  > to tenant > Tenant 1
  > from listing > Listing ?
  > has status > LeaseStatus 1
LeaseStatus | The state of a lease.
  * Active, Notice given, Expired, Terminated, Renewed
RentCharge | An amount due under a lease for a period.
  - period : string !
  - due date : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  > under lease > Lease 1
  > of type > ChargeType 1
ChargeType | The kind of charge.
  * Rent, Service charge, Utilities, Late fee
RentPayment | Money received from a tenant.
  - paid on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  > settles > RentCharge +
== Upkeep | Maintenance and valuation | Looking after it.
MaintenanceRequest | A reported need for repair or service in a unit.
  - raised on : date !
  - completed on : date
  - description : string !
  - cost : decimal
  > for unit > Unit 1
  > raised by > Tenant ?
  > in category > MaintenanceCategory 1
MaintenanceCategory | The trade involved.
  * Plumbing, Electrical, HVAC, Structural, Appliances, Cleaning
Valuation | An assessment of what a property or unit is worth.
  - valued on : date !
  - market value : decimal !
  - valuer : string
  > of property > Property ?
  > of unit > Unit ?
rule: derivation | Occupancy | Occupancy is let area divided by total lettable area. | Unit, Lease
rule: constraint | One active lease | A unit has at most one active lease at a time. | Lease, Unit
rule: derivation | Arrears | Arrears are rent charges past their due date less payments settling them. | RentCharge, RentPayment
rule: derivation | Gross yield | Gross yield is annual rent divided by market value. | Lease, Valuation
uc: Leases expiring | Leasing manager | Which leases expire in the next 90 days, and at what rent compared with asking rents? | Lease, Unit, Tenant, LeaseStatus | Lease.of unit, to tenant, Lease.has status, Lease.end date, Lease.monthly rent
uc: Rent arrears | Property manager | Which tenants owe rent past the due date, and how much? | RentCharge, RentPayment, Lease, Tenant | under lease, to tenant, settles, RentCharge.amount, RentCharge.due date
uc: Days on market | Sales director | How long do listings take to close, by property type and agent? | Listing, Unit, Building, Property, PropertyType, Agent | Listing.of unit, in building, on property, Property.of type, by agent, Listing.listed on, Listing.closed on
